WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:03.910
Data science teams work in
diverse technical environments

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:06.400
with many data
sources, coding tools,

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.670
computational requirements
and client expectations

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:11.260
for data products.

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.350
Having this work spread
across multiple systems

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:18.220
creates inefficient work silos
and introduces critical gaps

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.180
in security.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.910
RStudio Workbench
addresses all of this

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:27.390
by providing IT the
ability to manage and scale

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:32.759
data ingestion, analysis and
data product creation securely,

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:35.130
all from one place,
while providing

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:39.900
data scientists the ability
to collaborate on R and Python projects.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.140
Whether RStudio,
with its ability

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.630
to run multiple versions of R
in different sessions or Jupyter Lab

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.500
or Jupyter
Notebooks or VS code,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.890
each with the option of running
pre-configured data connectors,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:56.220
requesting compute resources
and providing the ability

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.400
to collaborate within
a shared environment.

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.400
If they choose to use
the RStudio IDE, team members

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.489
can share projects and
track work in real time,

00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:08.730
helping to keep up with changes
and supporting best practices

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.850
for code review, which
ultimately allows data science

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.340
leaders to build happy
and effective teams

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.950
while delivering value
to their stakeholders.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.740
Using RStudio Workbench,
the data science team

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:23.760
can create reports, dashboards
and interactive applications

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.010
for their organizations
decision makers,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:30.420
which can be hosted on
platforms such as RStudio Connect.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:32.640
By moving work
from the local laptop

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.430
and onto RStudio Workbench,

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:36.660
users can quickly
authenticate and spin up

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.830
the coding environment of their
choice for either R or Python,

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.740
providing easy access
to pre-configured data connectors

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.190
like Snowflake,
MongoDB and Spark,

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:50.070
just to name a few.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:53.250
Your team can also request
critical compute resources

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:56.220
that they won't likely have
access to on local systems

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:59.340
with different user or
group profiles for default

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:03.480
and max resource usage,
which helps to control cost.

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.280
RStudio Workbench
makes it easier

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.430
for teams to work together by
providing a standardized set

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:11.790
of installed software, which
helps ensure that data science work

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:14.610
is reproducible
between team members.

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:17.870
And integration with Git
supports collaboration and

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.150
code governance across
coding environments.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.630
RStudio Workbench:
Enable your team,

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:29.190
to build great data
science products.

